"_doc": [
  "The fish photo judgements (judging/FISH.md, the rubric): python3 tools/fish_judge.py writes them into fish-photos.json (e, jt).",
  "photos: teaching id -> {photo id (fish-photos.json f): code}. A code is view (p profile, o oblique, h head-on, t tail, d from above), whole (1, 0 partial),",
  "  light (g good, d dim or cast, n night or flash on black), clarity (s sharp, m soft, b blurred or murky), size (l large, m medium, s small),",
  "  count (1 one fish, s several of one kind, m other kinds too, x subject unclear), flags (j juvenile, c camouflage, a out of water), then the ease 1-5.",
  "  The tool adds the phase flag p for the entries fish.json marks dimorph, and caps the ease (judging/FISH.md \"Caps\").",
  "passes: who judged what, how, and when. A photo of fish-photos.json not listed here is not judged yet (no e: it starts at difficulty 0)."
],
